# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The model chain. Tried top to bottom until one answers; a tier is skipped
# entirely when its key is absent, so one key on its own is a valid setup.
#
# If every tier fails, the app still keeps the capture — saved verbatim and
# flagged unsorted, to be sorted later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 1. Google AI Studio. https://aistudio.google.com/apikey — a plain AIza...
#    string. Not an OAuth client id/secret: those sign users into Google
#    accounts and cannot authenticate Gemini calls.
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# 2. Groq. https://console.groq.com/keys — very fast, generous free tier.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# 3. OpenRouter. https://openrouter.ai/keys — one key reaching many models,
#    so it is the useful last resort. Set OPENROUTER_MODEL to any slug it
#    lists, including the free ones.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Single-user password gate. Leave unset and the gate is off, which is fine
# locally. Set it in production — an open /api/sort spends someone's quota.
# The login endpoint rate-limits by client address (5 attempts / 15 min).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_PASSWORD=
